---
layout: base.njk
title: Cyclometer — Coming soon to iPhone
bodyClass: home
---
<header class="hero">
  <img class="hero-photo"
       src="/assets/img/hero-1600.jpg"
       srcset="/assets/img/hero-1600.jpg 1600w, /assets/img/hero-2400.jpg 2400w"
       sizes="100vw"
       alt="A cyclist rides a road bike around a bend in a forest road">
  <div class="hero-content">
    <h1 class="wordmark"><img class="app-icon" src="/favicon.svg" alt="">{{ site.name }}</h1>
    <p class="tagline">{{ site.tagline }}</p>
    {% if site.appStoreUrl %}
    <a class="cta" href="{{ site.appStoreUrl }}">Download on the App Store</a>
    {% else %}
    <p class="cta cta-soon">Coming soon to the App Store</p>
    {% endif %}
  </div>
</header>
<main>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="section-inner">
      <p class="eyebrow">Built for the ride</p>
      <h2>Everything you need at a glance. Nothing you don't.</h2>
      <ul class="features">
        <li>
          <h3>Readable in full sun</h3>
          <p>Big, high-contrast numbers you can read with one glance, even with the screen dimmed.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h3>Radar alerts</h3>
          <p>Pair a Garmin Varia and see vehicles approaching from behind before you hear them.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h3>Your sensors, your zones</h3>
          <p>Connects to Bluetooth heart rate, speed, and cadence sensors. HR zones are set from your Apple Health data.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h3>Automatic wheel sizing</h3>
          <p>GPS calibrates your wheel so speed and distance from your sensor stay accurate.</p>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="section section-alt">
    <div class="section-inner">
      <p class="eyebrow">Private by design</p>
      <h2>Your rides stay on your iPhone.</h2>
      <ul class="features">
        <li>
          <h3>No account</h3>
          <p>No sign-up, no login, no backend. Open the app and ride.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h3>On-device history</h3>
          <p>Routes, heart rate, and ride history are stored only on your phone, and nothing is sold or shared for advertising.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h3>Share on your terms</h3>
          <p>Completed rides can be saved to Apple Health, and you can export any ride as a GPX file.</p>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>
</main>
<footer class="site-footer">
  <a href="/privacy-policy/">Privacy Policy</a>
  <span>Photo by <a href="{{ site.photo.url }}">{{ site.photo.credit }}</a> on Unsplash</span>
</footer>
